      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-08T20:59:58Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): mark a warned path's moves in the viewport and frame them from the op page\n\nEvery move a verify warning names (gouge, shank/holder, rapid in\nstock, fixture, crossing, envelope, sweep, scallop) now draws in the\ncolour-vision palette's gouge colour instead of its feed/rapid/plunge\ncolour, and the first move of each folded warning line carries a small\n3-axis cross in that colour. Each folded warning line on the op page's\nstatus banner is a link: a click centres the camera on that move\n(view state, no command, zoom kept).\n\nThe move set is a pure app function (app::warned_moves) over the cached\nwarning list; indices past the path's end are dropped, never indexed.\nRestUnjudged locates nothing and marks nothing. The per-path overlay\nloop moves out of interact.rs into ui::path_lines; a path with no\nwarnings draws exactly what it drew before.\n\nRefs #261\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
